<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan Treasury auction raises 1.186 bln dirhams.</title>
<headline>Moroccan Treasury auction raises 1.186 bln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan Treasury raised 1.186 billion dirhams from its weekly treasury bill auction, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rates and amounts (in million dirhams) were accepted as follows:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	 BID    AMOUNT		INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    26 weeks	 800     800			8.4  pct</p>
<p>    52 weeks	 xx	 xx			9.0  pct</p>
<p>    Two years	xx	 xx			9.5  pct</p>
<p>    Five years     100	100		    10.00 pct</p>
<p>    10 years	 100	100		    10.25 pct</p>
<p>    15 years	 186	186		    10.50 pct</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	    1,186     1,186</p>
<p>The next auction will take place on December 16, 1996, the bank said.</p>
<p>The commercial banks have reduced interest rate on 26-week bills to 8.4 percent from 8.5 percent in the previous auction, a bank official said. &quot;But this might change in the next auction,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>($1= 8.8 dirhams)</p>
<p>-- Rabat newsroom +212-7 726518</p>
